{
  "provenance": {
    "source": "docs/specs/O1-bridge-gateway-protocol.md (RBP/1 v1.0, frozen)",
    "sections": [
      "Section 11 invoke_batch request and batch_digest material (~835-903)",
      "Section 12.1 durable batch coordination binding (~1069-1075)",
      "Section 12.2 invoke_batch redelivery mismatch rules (~1100-1105)",
      "Section 21 item 30 golden vectors (~1512-1513)"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "The canonical vector payload and its batch_digest are copied verbatim from the frozen Section 11 example, including the step params_digest.",
      "Every changed-element vector pins the digest produced by the same RFC 8785 engine that reproduces the canonical spec digest; a changed vector digest must never equal the digest of its base vector, because on redelivery any changed element is a terminal protocol fault.",
      "step-omitted is byte-for-byte the canonical single-step material, so its digest equals the canonical digest and can never be mistaken for the two-step batch: no journal path reconstructs a batch from a prefix.",
      "property-reorder proves that harmless JSON property order reserialization yields the identical RFC 8785 value and digest."
    ]
  },
